 "_doc": "Smart objects / activity spots (scripts/living_world/smart_objects.gd). Object frame = Godot local space of the object: +Z is its FRONT (the side a worker normally uses), +X its right, +Y up. slots[].stand = where the character's root stands (object frame, metres); slots[].face = the direction the character faces, in degrees of yaw relative to the object's +Z (180 = facing the object). stand may be replaced by \"auto\": computed from the loop clip's sidecar anchor.at (the object's work-surface point relative to the character), so clip and spot always agree. approach = metres the character walks to first, straight out from the stand point along the slot's facing reversed (a clean line-up, then a short align). activity: enter / loop (list: variants chosen per cycle) / exit clips, between = one-shots sometimes played between loop cycles, cycles = how many loop cycles before a between/one-shot, duration = [min, max] seconds of use. Filters: jobs (WorldSim.JOBS names), acts (utility acts: work, shop, inn, pray, social, rest, eat, water, play, patrol), hours = [from, to) local hours, kids = true for children only / false adults only. capacity = number of slots. building_spots place objects around settlement lots / landmarks by their asset key (offsets in the building's frame: +Z = the building's front/door side).",
